From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paranoica <mitjumper@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:58:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(workspace-manager): give a monitor that comes back its
 workspaces and windows

When a monitor went away, its container was freed and a new one with fresh
workspaces was made when it came back. Its windows were moved to the active
workspace of another monitor and stayed there. Twin monitors that share the
vendor, product and serial also share the logical monitor id, so the
preferred monitor of a window could not tell them apart either.

Keep the container of a monitor that went away, detached, and hand it back
when a monitor with the same spec, connector included, appears again.
Remember the workspace each window was moved off, and put the window back
on it and on its monitor when the container returns, unless the window was
moved to another workspace or monitor in the meantime. While monitors
change, keep a window on the monitor of its workspace, and move the global
active workspace to the primary monitor when its own monitor went away.
